~ start
- Good Morning Sir, do you mind explaining to me what happened this morning ?
	Arrestee: It's as written in that report Mr. Officer. I was caught stealing a convenience store.
	Officer: I do see that but it's also your first offense. You quite strike me like an honest man. Why did you do that ?
	Arrestee: It’s hard to explain. You ever felt the world just closes in on you?
	Officer: Happens more than you think. Still, that’s no excuse for theft.
	Arrestee: Maybe not. But when you’ve got nothing left, you stop thinking straight.
	Officer: Alright, I get it. I see a lot of different cases in this post everyday after all. [wait=2] You look tired. 
	Arrestee: I didn’t plan any of this. I just needed to eat. Needed something to drink, maybe forget a little.
	Officer: *sighs* You’re not making my job any easier, you know that?
	- Your future now depends on me, but if you please me... I can help you get out of this.
		Arrestee: What do you mean, Sir?
		Officer: I’m saying, maybe I can make this whole thing disappear. If you can make it worth my time.
		Arrestee: Oh... I see. So that’s how it works.
		Officer: That’s how it works when people like you make it complicated. How ùuch do you have ?
		Arrestee: Then we understand each other, Sir. I have 10k on meright now.
	- You may have your circumstances, but I’ll have to do my job. You’ll have to take responsibility for your actions.
		Arrestee: I can’t object. My life is in your hands.
		Officer: For what it’s worth, I believe you didn’t mean harm. But the law’s the law.
		Arrestee: ...I guess I deserve what’s coming.
		Officer: Maybe. Or maybe this is where you start over.
		Officer: Guard, take him in. Treat him gently.
		Arrestee: Thank you, Officer. For treating me like a person.
		Officer: Let’s hope the system does the same.
- Why are you even here? Someone drag this guy in a cell already !!
	Arrestee: *shivers at your cruelty* 
	Officer: You think stealing is some kind of game?
	Arrestee: No, Sir! I was just hungry!
	Officer: Don’t talk unless I ask you to! You disgust me.
	Arrestee: Please... I didn’t hurt anyone...
	Officer: Oh, you didn’t hurt anyone? Tell that to the man whose store you stole from. 
	- I’ve heard enough. You’re done. You’ll rot in that cell until you learn respect.
		Arrestee: *weakly* Please... I don’t want to die in there...
		Officer: Should’ve thought of that before you stole. Guard! Take him away.
		Officer: Justice served — or maybe just another day at the office.
	- *pauses* ...You said you were hungry?
		Arrestee: Yes, Sir. I haven’t eaten in two days.
		Officer: Damn it... You really make this hard, you know that?
		Arrestee: I’m sorry. I’ll pay back, I swear.
		Officer: You’ll still spend the night here. But I’ll see what I can do in the morning.
		Arrestee: You mean... you’ll help me?
		Officer: Don’t thank me yet. You still broke the law. But maybe there’s still something left in you worth saving.
		Arrestee: Thank you, Sir. Truly.
		Officer: Don’t make me regret it.
	- *leans closer, lowering voice* You say you’ll pay back... how exactly?
		Arrestee: There might be... another way to settle this, Sir. Between us.
		Officer: Go on.
		Arrestee: I’m not asking for mercy. Just... understanding. I can make it worth your while.
		Officer: ...
		Arrestee: How about 10k
		Officer: ...
		Arrestee: We don’t need to write anything down, do we?
		Officer: I suppose not.
		Arrestee: Then... we understand each other.
=> END